---
import SectionHead from './ui/SectionHead.astro';

interface Props {
  num?: string;
}

const { num = '13' } = Astro.props;
---

<section id="lineage" class="lineage-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="lineage-top">
      <SectionHead num={num} kicker="Lineage" title="It Started With Fire★" />

      <div class="lineage-narrative">
        <p>
          In 2014 I released a project called <a href="https://firestr.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="fire-link">Fire★</a>,
          the <strong>Grass Computing Platform</strong>. It let people build peer-to-peer apps with a
          built-in collaborative editor. You'd create conversations and launch apps in them, and
          people could copy the apps and hack on them together. There was no cloud in the middle.
        </p>
        <p>
          It made things much easier, but people still needed to learn programming to use it to
          its fullest. Fire★ was written in C++ with apps in Lua.
        </p>
        <p class="lineage-last">
          Abject is its spiritual successor. It's the same idea with TypeScript and WASM, a canvas
          desktop, and an LLM that works out how objects that were never designed together can
          talk. This time you don't need to know programming to use it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="split evolution">
      <div class="evo evo-fire ghost">
        <p class="side-label">2014</p>
        <h3>Fire★</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>C++ / Qt / Lua</li>
          <li>RSA 4096 encryption</li>
          <li>Apps copied and shared by hand</li>
          <li>firelocator for peer discovery</li>
          <li><a href="https://firestr.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="evo-link">firestr.com</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rule evo-rule" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="evo-arrow"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="evo evo-abjects">
        <p class="side-label hand">Today</p>
        <h3>Abject</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>TypeScript / WASM / Canvas</li>
          <li>ECDSA/ECDH + AES-256-GCM</li>
          <li>Objects work out how to talk, with an LLM</li>
          <li>A signaling server introduces peers, then peers relay for each other</li>
          <li><span class="evo-link">abject.world</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lineage-top {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: 1rem 4rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 4.5rem;
  }

  .lineage-narrative p {
    color: var(--bone-2);
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .lineage-narrative strong { color: var(--bone-heading); }

  .lineage-narrative .lineage-last {
    color: var(--bone);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--red);
  }

  .fire-link { font-weight: 700; }

  /* The split: the ancestor ghosted on the left, Abject on the hand side. */
  .evolution {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 6px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }

  .evo h3 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.6rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }

  .evo-fire h3 { color: var(--brass); }
  .evo-abjects h3 { color: var(--bone-heading); }

  .evo ul { list-style: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-mid); }

  .evo li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--bone-2);
    padding: 0.55rem 0 0.55rem 1.3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    position: relative;
  }

  .evo li::before {
    content: '\25A0';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.62rem;
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--bone-faint);
  }

  .evo-abjects li::before { color: var(--red); }
  .evo-abjects li { color: var(--bone); }

  .evo-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--bone-meta);
  }

  a.evo-link { color: var(--living); }

  /* A big red wedge hung on the rule, pointing from the old to the new. */
  .evo-rule { position: relative; }

  .evo-arrow {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 42%;
    width: 64px;
    height: 76px;
    transform: translate(-40%, -50%);
    background: var(--red);
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 50%, 0 100%);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .lineage-top { grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .evolution { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .evo-rule { height: 6px; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    .evo-arrow {
      top: 50%;
      width: 56px;
      height: 44px;
      transform: translate(-50%, -30%);
      clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 50% 100%);
    }
  }
</style>
